TI  - Posterior tracheal diverticulosis.
PG  - 338-41
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000091 [doi]
AB  - Multiple tracheal diverticulosis is a rare clinical entity. Tracheal diverticula 
      are usually recognized radiologically as solitary right paratracheal air 
      collections on thoracic computed tomography examination. They are usually 
      asymptomatic but can occasionally present with persistent symptoms. We herein 
      report the case of a 50-year-old male patient who underwent extensive evaluation 
      for persistent cough. Multiple posterior right paratracheal air collections were 
      recognized on thoracic multidetector computed tomography examination, which was 
      confirmed as multiple-acquired posterior upper tracheal diverticula on flexible 
      bronchoscopy. The patient improved with conservative medical management.
