TI  - Bronchopulmonary sequestration in a 60 year old man.
PG  - 32-9
LID - 10.3941/jrcr.v8i10.2235 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of bronchopulmonary sequestration (BPS) in a 60 year old man 
      with recurrent cough. After failed antibiotic therapy for presumed left lower 
      lobe (LLL) pneumonia seen on chest radiographs, bronchoscopy was performed 
      revealing cryptogenic organizing pneumonia. Further work-up with thoracic imaging 
      demonstrates a feeding artery from the thoracic aorta to the LLL consolidation 
      indicating the presence of BPS. A brief review of the clinical and radiological 
      features and management options of BPS are listed, with particular emphasis on 
      the various imaging modalities and techniques in the diagnosis and pre-surgical 
      planning of intralobar sequestration.
