TI  - Pseudo-outbreak of Phaeoacremonium parasiticum from a hospital ice dispenser.
PG  - 1063-5
LID - 10.1086/677150 [doi]
AB  - In 31 patients, Phaeoacremonium parasiticum was recovered from bronchoscopy 
      specimens (biopsies and aspirates). The pseudo-outbreak was caused by 
      contaminated ice used to control hemorrhage during bronchoscopy and was 
      associated with deficiencies in equipment cleaning. The bronchoscopy technique 
      was modified, the ice dispenser was disinfected, bronchoscope reprocessing was 
      improved, and there were no recurrences.
