TI  - Electromagnetic navigation bronchoscopy for the diagnosis of Aspergillus 
      infection.
PG  - 30-2
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.39 [doi]
AB  - Electromagnetic navigation bronchoscopy (ENB) is a new diagnostic tool for the 
      evaluation of pulmonary lesions inaccessible by conventional bronchoscopy. Most 
      often, ENB is used for the diagnosis of lung cancer, but can be used to evaluate 
      fungal conditions and other diseases. We present the case of a 44-year-old woman 
      who was diagnosed with Aspergillus via ENB.
