DP  - 2014
TI  - Effectiveness and efficacy of minimally invasive lung volume reduction surgery 
      for emphysema.
PG  - Doc01
LID - 10.3205/hta000117 [doi]
LID - Doc01
AB  - Lung emphysema is a chronic, progressive and irreversible destruction of the lung 
      tissue. Besides non-medical therapies and the well established medical treatment 
      there are surgical and minimally invasive methods for lung volume reduction (LVR) 
      to treat severe emphysema. This report deals with the effectiveness and 
      cost-effectiveness of minimally invasive methods compared to other treatments for 
      LVR in patients with lung emphysema. Furthermore, legal and ethical aspects are 
      discussed. No clear benefit of minimally invasive methods compared to surgical 
      methods can be demonstrated based on the identified and included evidence. In 
      order to assess the different methods for LVR regarding their relative 
      effectiveness and safety in patients with lung emphysema direct comparative 
      studies are necessary.
