TI  - [Anomalous systemic arterial supply to left basal lung with anomalous return of 
      V6].
PG  - 1060-3
AB  - The patient was 52-year-old woman. Her chief compliant was bloody sputum. The 
      computed tomography revealed an anomalous artery from descending aorta running 
      into left lung basal segment and anomalous left V6 return to superior pulmonary 
      vein. The bronchoscopic examination showed normal bronchial branches. Under the 
      diagnosis of anomalous systemic arterial supply to left basal lung without 
      sequestration, left lower lobectomy was performed. Microscopically, the pulmonary 
      artery showed intimal thickening and alveolar collapse with interstitial fibrosis 
      were seen. The postoperative course was uneventful and she discharged at 6th 
      postoperative day.
