TI  - Tailored stent for bronchial stump fistula closure and omentoplasty for infection 
      control: a combined approach with low morbidity.
PG  - 157e-9e
LID - 10.1700/1636.17938 [doi]
AB  - Bronchopleural fistula (BPF) after pneumonectomy remains a dangerous complication 
      with high mortality and morbidity. Primary closure of the fistula with muscle 
      flaps and a thoracic window is generally used to treat BPF. New techniques for 
      secondary stump closure including glues, stents and coils have been introduced 
      recently. We report the use of a J-shaped tracheal stent device placed during 
      bronchoscopy combined with omentoplasty to control the symptoms related to BPF 
      and pleural space infection, respectively.
