TI  - Occult interferon α-induced pulmonary granulomatosis despite continuation of 
      treatment.
PG  - 1012-6
LID - 10.5414/CP202125 [doi]
AB  - Interferon alpha (IFN α)-based treatment of chronic hepatitis C viral (HCV) 
      infection may induce pulmonary and extrapulmonary sarcoidosis. We report a case 
      of a 50-year-old male patient who suffered from hepatitis C-induced liver 
      cirrhosis with respiratory insufficiency due to severe hepatopulmonary syndrome. 
      After 9 months of treatment with IFNα and ribavirin, he developed an 
      asymptomatic, clinically occult pulmonary granulomatosis, which was not 
      detectable in CT. The diagnosis was made by bronchoscopy with bronchoalveolar 
      lavage and transbronchial lung biopsy. The condition did not progress to 
      clinically apparent disease despite continuation of IFN alpha treatment.
