TI  - Tablet in the bronchus--an unusual cause for persistent cough in a 64 year old 
      gentleman.
PG  - 63-5
AB  - Foreign body aspiration in adults without any background risk factors is 
      uncommon. We report a 64 year gentleman evaluated for persistent cough 
      incidentally detected to have a foreign body (FB) in the left main bronchus 
      (LMB), which after removal by rigid bronchoscopy turned out to be a tablet. This 
      demonstrates the possible risk of silent aspiration of solid foreign bodies and 
      in our case presenting as a persistent cough after months of aspiration. 
      Bronchoscopic evaluation should be carried out in the differential diagnosis of 
      persistent or recurrent pulmonary symptoms.
