TI  - Complete transection of the left main bronchus caused by blunt thoracic trauma in 
      a child treated by bronchoplasty and lung parenchyma preservation.
PG  - 113-5
LID - 10.1007/s11748-014-0448-0 [doi]
AB  - Blunt bronchial injuries can be difficult to diagnose and can present months or 
      years after an initial incident. The present case report describes complete 
      transection of a major airway after a potentially fatal delayed diagnosis with a 
      successful outcome after bronchoplasty without the removal of lung parenchyma.
