AB  - We report a 68-year-old female who presented with chronic cough and progressive 
      dyspnoea. Computed tomography of the thorax and subsequent bronchoscopy confirmed 
      the diagnosis of pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (PAP), which was treated with 
      whole lung lavage. This case is reported in view of the low incidence of PAP.
