TI  - An unexpected oesophageal web in a case of suspected tracheo-oesophageal fistula 
      in a premature neonate posted for diagnostic broncho-oesophagoscopy.
PG  - 344-6
AB  - Oesophageal webs are thin (2-3mm) membranes of normal oesophageal tissue 
      consisting of mucosa and submucosa. They can be congenital or acquired. 
      Congenital oesophageal webs are very rare and usually present in adulthood. This 
      report describes an unusual presentation of congenital web in lower oesophagus in 
      a premature neonate with respiratory distress who was posted for diagnostic 
      bronchoscopy and oesophagoscopy under general anaesthesia to rule out 
      tracheo-oesophageal fistula or tracheomalacia. Endoscopic dilatation of the web 
      was done and the baby improved after the procedure.
