TI  - [Bronchial hamartoma in subsegmental bronchus; report of a case].
PG  - 169-71
AB  - We report a rare surgical case of a bronchial hamartoma in subsegmental bronchus. 
      A 70-year-old man was incidentally pointed out an abnormal chest shadow without 
      any complaints. Chest computed tomography revealed a round nodule with diameter 
      of 15 mm in the right upper lobe. The bronchoscopic examination revealed complete 
      obstruction of right B2a by the tumor. Right S2 segmentectomy was done to make a 
      definite diagnosis and to prevent possible obstructive pneumonia. 
      Histopathological examination revealed that the tumor was a benign cartilage 
      bronchial hamartoma.
