TI  - [Expectoration of embolization coils 15 years after embolization of pulmonary 
      arteriovenous malformations in a patient with hereditary hemorrhagic 
      telangiectasia].
PG  - 282-5
LID - 10.1055/s-0034-1365127 [doi]
AB  - Hereditary hemorrhagic telangiectasia can manifest itself with pulmonary 
      arteriovenous malformations (pavm). A transcatheter coil embolization should be 
      made to avoid complications and to close off relevant arteriovenous shunts. We 
      report on a patient with expectoration of embolization coils 15 years after 
      embolotherapy. In case of hemoptysis following embolotherapy with coils, even 
      years after their placement one should consider coil migration into the pulmonary 
      system, besides newly formed pavms, in the differential diagnosis and initiate 
      contrast-CT of the thorax and bronchoscopy.
