TI  - [Experience of medical assistance in the hosital of Plesetsk Cosmodrome under 
      conditions of large patient load after explosion of a launch vehicle].
PG  - 79-82
AB  - Military hospital of Plesetsk Cosmodrome was founded on 20 December 1958. The 
      aims of the hospital were always connected with medical support of the 
      cosmodrome, including emergency situations. On 18 March 1980 a Vostok-2M rocket 
      exploded on its launch pad during a fuelling operation. Experience of medical 
      assistance under conditions of large patient load showed the necessity of 
      constant readiness to medical assistance to patients with combined pathology 
      (burn injury, orthopedic trauma and thermochemical injury of the upper 
      respiratory tract), expediency of compact patient accommodation along with the 
      modern anaesthetic machine and readiness to frequent suction bronchoscopy.
