TI  - All that wheezes is not asthma.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2013-202369 [doi]
LID - bcr2013202369
AB  - A young woman was admitted with respiratory failure. Prior to her admission, she 
      had been treated for clinical bronchial asthma for about 2 years for recurrent 
      wheezing. Endotracheal intubation was difficult. A fibroptic bronchoscopy, while 
      the patient was ventilated, revealed a central tracheal tumour compromising >90% 
      of the tracheal lumen. The tumour was cored out during rigid bronchoscopy while 
      ventilating the patient through tracheostomy. Histopathology of the tumour was 
      suggestive of adenoid cystic carcinoma.
