TI  - [Pulmonary sclerosing hemangioma with lymph node metastasis].
PG  - 1141-4
AB  - Sclerosing hemangioma is unusual pulmonary tumor. During a routine care 
      evaluation, an abnormal shadow was detected in the chest X-ray films of a 
      38-year-old woman. Chest computed tomography scanning showed a nodule, 3.9 cm in 
      diameter, in the left S6 pulmonary segment. Bronchoscopy performed before the 
      operation could not establish the diagnosis. Since low-grade malignant tumor 
      wassuggested by frozen section analysis at surgery, segmentectomy of left S6 and 
      sampling of interlober lymph node were performed. The tumor was diagnosed as a 
      plmonary sclerosing hemangioma. Metastatic leasion in the interlober lymph node 
      was pathologically confirmed.
