TI  - Endobronchial lipoma.
PG  - 784-5
AB  - Endobronchial lipomas are rare benign tumours of the lung. The reported case was 
      a 56-year-old man who visited the public hospital with complaints of chest pain 
      and persistent cough. On bronchoscopy, a smooth-surfaced polypoid tumour 
      obstructing the main bronchus in the left lobe was detected. The case was 
      evaluated and surgical resection was performed. Histopathological investigation 
      revealed that the tumour was an endobronchial lipoma; the tumour composed of 
      mature fat tissue and was covered with bronchial epithelium.
