TI  - Pulmonary resection for bronchial polyp after lung transplant in a cystic 
      fibrosis patient.
PG  - 81-4
LID - 10.6002/ect.2012.0300 [doi]
AB  - Many clinical conditions should be considered in the differential diagnosis of 
      life-threatening events in cystic fibrosis patients after a lung graft 
      transplant. We report on a 17-year-old boy who underwent a lobectomy owing to an 
      inflammatory endobronchial polyp complicated by massive airways bleeding 12 
      months after having had a bilateral sequential lung graft for cystic fibrosis. 
      This unusual complication underscores the requirement for flexible bronchoscopy 
      in patients with recurrent infection at any stage after transplant. Early 
      diagnosis may prevent life-threatening complications.
