TI  - Aspiration of a cigarette filter from a bronchodilator inhaler.
PG  - e39-41
LID - 10.4187/respcare.01898 [doi]
AB  - The majority of foreign-body aspirations are seen in children. In adults, 
      neurological dysfunction, trauma, alcohol abuse, or psychological disorders can 
      lead to aspiration, but normal adults can also suffer foreign body aspiration. 
      The symptoms include acute asphyxiation, with or without complete airway 
      obstruction, cough, dyspnea, choking, and fever, which also occur in many other 
      medical conditions. Bronchoscopic removal of the foreign body is necessary, and 
      flexible bronchoscopy is effective in the diagnosis and removal. We saw a patient 
      with COPD who aspirated a plastic cigarette filter while using his bronchodilator 
      inhaler.
