TI  - [Postoperatively increased oxygen demand and hemoptysis after extubation].
PG  - 147-50
LID - 10.1007/s00063-011-0043-4 [doi]
AB  - A 22-year-old man on postoperative day 1 after open reduction with internal 
      fixation of a distal fibula fracture presented with hemoptysis and increased 
      oxygen demand. X-ray and contrast-enhanced computed tomography revealed bilateral 
      patchy opacities and mediastinal emphysema. After bronchoscopy and 
      bronchoalveolar lavage, a diagnosis of alveolar hemorrhage was made. The medical 
      history revealed regular abuse of marihuana and cocaine.
