TI  - Balloon bronchoplasty: case series.
PG  - 42-8
AB  - Central airway stenosis may be a manifestation of benign or malignant lesions and 
      can be a life threatening condition. There are different surgical and endoscopic 
      modalities for treatment of these lesions. Balloon bronchoscopy is an 
      interventional pulmonologic modality and can be performed under direct vision or 
      fluoroscopic guidance. This technique can be used along with other interventional 
      modalities for treatment of patients with tracheal stenosis. In this study we 
      report balloon bronchoscopy as an interventional modality in a series of patients 
      with tracheal stenosis and assess the outcome.
