TI  - Endobronchial echinococcosis presenting as non-resolving pneumonia.
PG  - 716-8
LID - 10.1002/ppul.21597 [doi]
AB  - Hydatid disease of the lungs is caused by larval cysts of the Echinococcus 
      tapeworm. Pulmonary cysts may occasionally invade bronchi or pleura as a result 
      of coughing, trauma, or elevated intra-abdominal pressure. We present the case of 
      a patient evaluated for non-resolving pneumonia whose radiographic and 
      bronchoscopic findings were strikingly similar to those seen in pulmonary 
      tuberculosis with endobronchial invasion; he was ultimately diagnosed with 
      pulmonary echinococcosis. This case underscores the importance of considering 
      unusual diagnoses even when typical features of more common conditions are 
      present.
