TI  - Anesthetic considerations of central airway obstruction.
PG  - 326-8
LID - 10.4103/1658-354X.84113 [doi]
AB  - Central airway obstruction (CAO) is a serious presentation of lung cancer and 
      associated chest diseases. It presents a real challenge to the anesthesiologist 
      because usually the patient admitted to the hospital as an emergency case with 
      high grade dyspnea scheduled to undergo rigid bronchoscopy for diagnostic and 
      possible therapeutic interventions. In this case report, we described the 
      anesthetic management of a patient who was admitted to our hospital with CAO.
