TI  - Lung nodule management: a new classification proposal.
PG  - 223-34
AB  - Management of solitary pulmonary nodule (SPN) and micronodule (SPMN) is still 
      debated. The use of 18F-FDG PET/CT or CT multislice screening for early lung 
      cancer detection, have increased the frequency of displaying indeterminate single 
      lung nodule with diameter between 0.1 cm and 2 cm. The first choice is to wait 
      and do radiological follow-up, since the evaluation of temporal changes in a 
      small mass may contribute to differentiate a malign from benign pathology. In 
      case of unchanged images not capable of orientating the diagnostician or no 
      possible preoperative diagnosis by bronchoscopy and percutaneous needle biopsy, 
      surgical treatment is necessary allowing the histological characterization of 
      lesion and a good prognosis of disease. Video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery and 
      muscle-sparing minithoracotomy have become routine, each of these furnishing 
      precise indications. The purpose of the study was to establish the main 
      investigative method for indeterminate lung nodules, considering the continuous 
      evolution of endoscopic and radiological techniques.
