DP  - 2011 May
TI  - [Pleomorphic carcinoma of the lung; report of a case].
PG  - 426-9
AB  - A 83-year-old male was referred to our hospital for further examination of 
      abnormal shadow on chest radiography. Chest computed tomography (CT) showed a 
      tumor mass in his right lung. Bronchoscopy brushing cytology revealed non-small 
      cell lung carcinoma and right middle lobectomy was performed. Histological 
      findings showed large cell carcinoma comprised of spindle cell component, finally 
      diagnosing as pleomorphic carcinoma of the lung. Although he was diagnosed as 
      pT2N0M0 (stage IA) after the operation, massive liver metastasis was found 7 
      months later. We report this case with references to the literatures on 
      pleomorphic carcinoma of the lung.
