TI  - Primary pulmonary mucinous cystadenocarcinoma: a case report.
PG  - 562026
LID - 10.1155/2011/562026 [doi]
LID - 562026
AB  - Primary pulmonary mucinous cystadenocarcinoma (PMCAC) is an extremely rare cystic 
      neoplasm. A case of a 56-year-old male with a cystic lesion of the right lower 
      lobe is described. Preoperative fine needle aspiration cytology and bronchoscopy 
      were inconclusive. The patient underwent a formal right lower lobectomy and 
      mediastinal lymph node dissection. Diagnosis was established intraoperatively. 
      The biological behavior of primary PMCAC is unknown. Therefore, careful long-term 
      follow-up is considered necessary because of lack of experience globally.
