TI  - Sand aspiration: a case report and review of the radiological features and 
      management.
PG  - 848-54
LID - 10.1111/j.1365-2044.2010.06405.x [doi]
AB  - We report a case of severe sand aspiration in association with near-drowning, 
      which led to respiratory failure secondary to the acute respiratory distress 
      syndrome, necessitating mechanical ventilation, repeated therapeutic 
      bronchoscopic lavage, and a stay in the intensive care unit that exceeded one 
      month.
