TI  - Paraneoplastic sensorimotor neuropathy associated with regression of small cell 
      lung carcinoma.
LID - 10.1136/bcr.01.2009.1486 [doi]
LID - bcr0120091486
AB  - An elderly female smoker presented with nausea and anorexia. Imaging and 
      histopathology were consistent with a diagnosis of small cell lung cancer (SCLC). 
      She subsequently developed a progressive sensorimotor neuropathy with high titres 
      of anti-Hu antibodies. Development of the neuropathy was associated with marked 
      regression in the lung neoplasm. Repeat investigation with radioimaging and 
      bronchoscopy showed no evidence of neoplasia. Paraneoplastic sensorimotor 
      neuropathies are commonly associated with SCLC particularly in the presence of 
      anti-Hu antibodies. Regression of SCLC with anti-Hu antibodies has only been 
      reported twice previously. The authors believe this case supports the theory that 
      anti-Hu antibodies confer anti-tumour activity causing tumour regression.
