VI  - 27
IP  - 4
DP  - 2014 Aug
TI  - Anesthesia for bronchoscopy.
PG  - 453-7
LID - 10.1097/ACO.0000000000000087 [doi]
AB  - PURPOSE OF REVIEW: To discuss the recent advances in sedation and anesthesia for 
      the practice of both flexible and rigid bronchoscopy, which are increasingly 
      performed outside of the operating room by interventional pulmonologists and 
      thoracic surgeons. RECENT FINDINGS: Studies have recently documented the 
      advantages of pharmacological sedatives and anesthetics for use in bronchoscopy. 
      In particular, we review the increasing body of literature highlighting the 
      advantages and benefits of propofol anesthesia for both flexible and rigid 
      bronchoscopy. SUMMARY: As our practice expands, relocation of appropriately 
      triaged pulmonary interventional procedures including rigid bronchoscopy that 
      were previously assigned to a traditional operating room setting improves 
      provider flexibility, presents more cost-effective options while maintaining 
      patient safety and satisfaction and reducing the time to recovery. Anesthesia 
      practice has, therefore, shifted to caring for these sick patients outside the 
      operating room and increasingly cooperation between anesthesiologist and 
      proceduralist is required.
