TI  - Bronchoscopic topical steroid instillation in prevention of tracheal stenosis.
PG  - 91-3
LID - 10.4103/0970-9185.125712 [doi]
AB  - Corrosive acid poisoning commonly results in chemical injuries to respiratory and 
      upper gastrointestinal tract. Corrosive mucosal erosion of the larynx and trachea 
      may occur if the patient aspirates acid. We successfully used local 
      anti-inflammatory action of dexamethasone instilled through a fiber-optic 
      bronchoscope for regression of mucosal edema and prevention of subsequent 
      development of stricture in a young female.
