TI  - [Circulatory disturbance of middle lobe by bending of lobar pedicle after right 
      upper lobectomy].
PG  - 1079-82
AB  - A 66-year-old man was diagnosed as lung cancer. We performed right upper 
      lobectomy and lymphnode dissection. On the 1st postoperative day, a chest 
      radiograph showed an opacification in the right upper lung field. Computed 
      tomography (CT) showed a stenosis of the middle lobe bronchus and infiltrative 
      shadow of the middle lobe on the 3rd postoperative day. Fiber optic bronchoscopic 
      examination also revealed a bend and stenosis of the middle lobe bronchus, but 
      tortion was not demonstrated. On the 6th postoperative day, chest radiographic 
      findings was worsened. Torsion of the middle lobe was suspected, and 
      rethoracotomy was performed on the 7th postoperative day. The right middle lobe 
      was not rotated, but the lobar pedicle bend toward cranial. The middle lobe was 
      highly congested necessitating lobectomy.
