TI  - About a submucosal tracheal tumor.
PG  - 229
LID - 10.1186/1477-7819-11-229 [doi]
AB  - The authors report the case of 46-year-old man with recurrent hemoptysis. 
      Bronchoscopy revealed a submucosal tumor protruding into the tracheal lumen. 
      Transbronchial biopsy failed to obtain a conclusive diagnosis; only surgery 
      allowed complete resection of the tumor and confirmed the diagnosis of tracheal 
      mucoepidermoid carcinoma. We discuss the unusual submucosal presentation of this 
      tumor, and the contribution of surgery for diagnosis and therapy.
