AB  - Although bronchoscopy technology continues to evolve at a fairly rapid pace, 
      basic procedures, such as bronchoalveolar lavage, transbronchial lung biopsy, and 
      transbronchial needle aspiration, continue to play a paramount role in the 
      diagnosis of bronchopulmonary diseases. Pulmonologists should be trained in these 
      basic bronchoscopic procedures.
