TI  - Using Proseal LMA and I-gel for difficult airway management in patient with 
      diffuse tracheal stenosis and pulmonary artery sling.
PG  - 418-20
AB  - Pulmonary artery sling (PAS) is a rare congenital anomaly frequently accompanied 
      by focal or long-segment tracheal stenosis. We presented a 34-year-old female 
      patient with severe long-segment tracheal stenosis associated with PAS which was 
      assessed with Multi Slice Computed Tomography (MSCT) consisting of axial, three 
      dimensional and virtual bronchoscopic images of the airway. This case report 
      discussed the management of her difficult airway condition during surgical 
      cholecystectomy and thyroidectomy by using proseal- LMA and I-gel, respectively 
      (Fig. 4, Ref. 10).
