AB  - Rhinosporidiosis is a chronic granulomatous disease caused by Rhinosporidium 
      seeberi. We report a rare case of rhinosporidiosis, with involvement of the skin, 
      nasal cavity, larynx, oropharynx, and the bronchial tree. The patient underwent 
      bronchoscopic electrocautery excision of the endobronchial lesion with good 
      symptomatic improvement.
