DP  - 2013 Jan
TI  - Endobronchial ultrasound for peripheral lesions: a review.
PG  - 3-6
LID - 10.7178/eus.04.002 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is one of the most common tumors worldwide. Pulmonary lesions 
      detected during screening for lung cancer need to be evaluated further and tissue 
      should be obtained. Bronchoscopy is often the first step to secure a histological 
      diagnosis. Differ-ent guidance techniques are available to increase the 
      diagnostic yield. Over the last few years endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) has 
      been used increasingly to direct the sampling tools, often in combination with a 
      guide sheath. This article offers a review of the literature of the use of EBUS 
      in diagnosis of pulmonary peripheral lesions.
