TI  - Pulmonary lobectomy on delayed inhaled foreign body in adult: a case report.
PG  - 475-7
AB  - We present the case of a 51 years old female who experienced foreign body 
      aspiration 3 years before. The foreign body, which should be removed by 
      bronchoscopy before, was lodged at the bifurcation of the right inferior bronchus 
      and could only be removed via right lower lobectomy. The patient experienced a 
      swift recovery and was well at follow-up 8 months later.
