TI  - Aspiration of capsule endoscope and successful bronchoscopic extraction.
PG  - 328-31
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31826e3b53 [doi]
AB  - Capsule endoscopy is a novel tool for the diagnosis of small intestinal 
      disorders. Recently, a new complication of the procedure in the form of the 
      capsule's aspiration into the lungs has been reported. The aspiration of capsule 
      endoscope can lead to a variety of complications including respiratory failure. A 
      low threshold to suspect this complication and urgent bronchoscopic extraction in 
      appropriate patients can prevent serious sequelae.
