TI  - Respiratory review of 2012: bronchoscopic innovations and advances.
PG  - 197-203
LID - 10.4046/trd.2012.73.4.197 [doi]
AB  - Recent advances in bronchoscopy have led to changes in clinical diagnostics and 
      therapeutics in pulmonary medicine. In diagnostic bronchoscopy, there have also 
      been new developments in endobronchial ultrasound technology which may be 
      incorporated into clinical practice in the near future. Functional bronchoscopy, 
      which evaluates information such as airway pressure, airflow, or gas exchange, 
      suggests promising clinical advances in the near future. In therapeutic 
      bronchoscopy, bronchoscopic volume reduction is a novel approach for the 
      treatment of severe emphysema. In this review, seven recently published articles 
      representing current advances in bronchoscopy are summarized and discussed.
