TI  - Solitary rectal metastasis from primary small cell lung carcinoma.
PG  - 284-286
LID - 10.1111/j.1759-7714.2011.00091.x [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer may rarely appear with a solitary rectal metastasis and no other 
      metastases. We report the first case of primary small cell lung cancer presenting 
      with a solitary rectal metastasis in a 62-year-old man. Chest computed tomography 
      revealed a soft tissue lesion in the subcarinal area. Following bronchoscopic 
      biopsy, the patient was diagnosed with small cell lung cancer. The rectal mass 
      was incidentally found during an imaging study for staging work-up. Histological 
      examination revealed that the rectal mass was consistent with metastasis from 
      small cell lung cancer. We suggest that clinicians should consider the 
      possibility of rectal metastasis in small cell lung cancer patients with rectal 
      masses.
