TI  - Anesthetic management of an adult patient with Rett syndrome and limited mouth 
      opening -A case report-.
PG  - 428-30
LID - 10.4097/kjae.2011.61.5.428 [doi]
AB  - Rett syndrome is a neurological disease that occurs only in females and it 
      manifests with mental retardation, seizures, movement disorders, autistic 
      behavior and abnormal breathing. A 19-year-old female with Rett syndrome 
      underwent ophthalmologic surgery under general anesthesia at our institution. 
      Airway control was difficult due to her limited mouth opening. We recommend that 
      anesthesiologists should have proper knowledge about this disease and the 
      patients to avoid the complications and problems that can be encountered during 
      the perioperative period.
