TI  - Ventilator-associated Acinetobacter baumannii pneumonia.
PG  - 964-6
AB  - We report an outbreak of ventilator-associated pneumonia caused by 
      carbapenem-resistant Acinetobacter baumannii in 6 infants with acute lower 
      respiratory tract infection. Non-bronchoscopic bronchoalveolar lavage isolated A. 
      baumannii in all these infants. Environmental microbiological survey of the 
      Pediatric intensive care unit and pediatric wards identified oxygen humidifying 
      chambers as the source of Acinetobacter. Practices of cleaning and changing of 
      the humidifiers were reviewed and the outbreak was controlled with new 
      recommendations.
