TI  - Intraoperative bronchoscopy for bronchial carcinoid parenchymal-sparing 
      resection: a pediatric case report.
PG  - 75-8
LID - 10.1007/s00383-011-2940-2 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial carcinoid tumors are the most common primary pulmonary neoplasm in the 
      pediatric population. The widely accepted treatment for carcinoid tumors is 
      surgical, specifically aiming at being as much as conservative on lung 
      parenchyma, while the entire tumor is resected. A brief case is described, 
      highlighting the importance and advantages of a surgical and endoscopic combined 
      approach.
