TI  - Congenital lobar emphysema in an adult.
PG  - 67-9
LID - 10.4103/0970-2113.76307 [doi]
AB  - Congenital lobar emphysema (CLE) is a clinico-radiological diagnosis, seen 
      usually by four-six weeks of age (50% of patients) and rarely (<5% of patients) 
      after the age of six months. Here, we report a young male with gradual onset of 
      mild exertional breathlessness and physical examination revealing the features of 
      right sided pneumothorax. X-ray of chest, with subsequent CT of chest, leads to 
      the diagnosis of CLE. The pulmonary function tests, bronchoscopic examination and 
      α(1)-antitrypsin level are normal. Patient is managed conservatively.
