DP  - 2011 Apr
TI  - [Intubating laryngeal mask airway for fiberoptic bronchoscopy in a woman with 
      right bronchial tumor].
PG  - 454-7
AB  - A 37-year-old woman with bronchial tumor was scheduled for the removal of the 
      mass with fiberoptic bronchoscope. Intubating laryngeal mask airway (ILMA) was 
      used for fiberoptic surgery. Through a size 3 ILMA, a 5.9 mm outer diameter 
      fiberoptic bronchoscope reached the trachea easily. The operation was 
      successfully performed with assisted ventilation. Intraoperative laryngospasm was 
      treated with intravenous suxamethonium. The ILMA allowed removal of the bronchial 
      tumor with fiberoptic bronchoscope.
