TI  - Hypersensitivity pneumonitis associated with inhalation of catechin-rich green 
      tea extracts.
PG  - 388-92
LID - 10.1159/000324450 [doi]
AB  - A 51-year-old man presented with fever and fatigue after 3.5 months of 
      antituberculosis therapy. High-resolution computed tomography of his chest 
      revealed new ground-glass opacities and poorly defined centrilobular nodules. He 
      had undergone catechin inhalation for 1 month. We diagnosed hypersensitivity 
      pneumonitis (HP) based on the clinical course, bronchoscopy and a challenge test. 
      Cases of HP due to inhalation of extracted catechin powder are rare. Although it 
      has many known positive attributes, it is necessary to be aware that catechin can 
      cause HP.
