TI  - Tracheobronchial amyloidosis and confocal endomicroscopy.
PG  - 209-11
LID - 10.1159/000324256 [doi]
AB  - Tracheobronchial amyloidosis is one of many causes of endobronchial stenosis and 
      nodularity, the concrete diagnosis of which currently requires the finding of 
      apple-green birefringence from endobronchial biopsies. Bronchoscopic probe-based 
      confocal endomicroscopy (pCLE) is a novel optical biopsy technique which provides 
      real-time images of the lattice structure of the bronchial basement membrane - a 
      finding lost in malignancy. This case study outlines the imperfect, essentially 
      palliative management of this rare disease, and shows for the first time the 
      unusual dappled in vivo pCLE images of amyloid-affected endobronchium.
