TI  - Diffuse cylindrical bronchiectasis due to eosinophilic bronchopneumopathy in a 
      dog.
PG  - 753-6
AB  - A miniature pinscher-cross was evaluated for chronic coughing. Computed 
      tomography and bronchoscopy revealed severe, diffuse, cylindrical bronchiectasis 
      secondary to eosinophilic bronchopneumopathy. Computed tomography is the gold 
      standard for diagnosis of bronchiectasis in humans, and should be further 
      investigated in dogs as a means of characterizing severity and pattern of 
      disease.
