TI  - [Serious and consecutive airway complications after lung transplantation].
PG  - 367-70
AB  - Airway complications are relatively frequent after lung transplantation and 
      represent a great challenge to the medical team. In spite of the development of 
      different modalities of bronchoscopic treatment and a lower incidence of 
      complications with new surgical techniques, morbidity and mortality are still 
      elevated. We present the case of a woman who underwent right lung transplantation 
      who afterward developed four severe and consecutive airway complications that 
      solved with a successful therapy approach.
