TI  - General anesthesia in a patient with known bronchial anthracofibrosis -A case 
      report-.
PG  - 307-10
LID - 10.4097/kjae.2010.58.3.307 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial anthracosis was recently defined in the English radiology literature as 
      a luminal narrowing associated with anthracotic pigmentation on bronchoscopy 
      without a relevant history of pneumoconiosis or smoking. Anthracosis refers to 
      the presence of carbon particles in the lungs, not to a disorder per se. 
      Anthracofibrotic lesions carry the potential risk of massive hemorrhage during 
      endobronchial procedures. This report describes a case of general anesthesia for 
      a left modified radical mastectomy due to an intraductal carcinoma in a patient 
      with known bronchial anthracofibrosis.
