TI  - Primary tracheal non-Hodgkin lymphoma: case report with an emphasis on computed 
      tomography findings.
PG  - W24-6
LID - 10.1097/RTI.0b013e31819d5bfa [doi]
AB  - A 24-year-old male presented with productive cough associated with fever, 
      dyspnea, and hoarseness. A chest radiograph showed nonhomogeneous air-space 
      consolidations, mainly in the middle and inferior zones of both lungs, with 
      cavitations and peribronchial thickening. The computed tomography scan 
      demonstrated irregular, lobulated narrowing of the trachea, and parenchymal 
      consolidations containing air bronchogram, peribronchial thickening, and 
      cavitations. Afterward, the patient was referred for a bronchoscopy with a biopsy 
      of the tracheal mucosa. The samples were submitted to immunohistochemical 
      analysis and revealed a diagnosis of diffuse large B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma of 
      the trachea. A culture of bronchoalveolar lavage fluid revealed Pseudomonas 
      aeruginosa. Antibiotic treatment was proposed as a first treatment. The patient 
      did not receive intensive chemotherapy because of his comorbid conditions and 
      died 2 months later.
