DP  - 2010 Jan-Feb
TI  - Endoscopic sealing of bronchopleural fistulas with submucosal injection of a 
      tissue expander: a novel technique.
PG  - e23-4
AB  - The occurrence of a bronchopleural fistula (BPF) continues to represent a 
      challenging management problem, and is associated with high morbidity and 
      mortality. A novel and successful technique that uses submucosal injection of a 
      tissue expander for bronchoscopic occlusion of BPFs has been designed. This 
      method may be used either alone or in combination with bronchoscopic instillation 
      of n-butyl-cyanoacrylate glue. The occlusion technique is described, with a 
      presentation of two patients who were successfully treated with this method. The 
      submucosal injection of a tissue expander is an effective, economical and 
      minimally invasive technique for managing BPFs.
