TI  - Tracheal ring herniation.
PG  - 54-5
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181c7fe9c [doi]
AB  - Inspection bronchoscopy during percutaneous dilational tracheostomy has become 
      the standard of care to reduce complications of the procedure. During 
      bronchoscopy, anatomic defects can be visualized before performing the procedure. 
      We describe a case of discovering herniated tracheal rings in preprocedure 
      bronchoscopy and subsequent treatment of this rare finding.
