TI  - A rarely seen mucoepidermoid carcinoma of the left main bronchus.
PG  - 384-6
LID - 10.4103/0973-1482.136665 [doi]
AB  - Mucoepidermoid carcinomas (MEC) are rare malignant tumors that originate in the 
      submucosal bronchial glands, and complete resection usually correlates with 
      favorable prognosis. A 54-year-old male patient was diagnosed with high-grade MEC 
      in the left main bronchus via bronchoscopy. After the patient was diagnosed with 
      metastatic lung cancer, chemotherapy was started. Two years after the diagnosis, 
      the patient is still alive.
