TI  - Endotracheal tube intubation with the aid of a laryngeal mask airway, a 
      fiberoptic bronchoscope, and a tube exchanger in a difficult airway patient: a 
      case report.
PG  - 237-9
LID - 10.4097/kjae.2014.66.3.237 [doi]
AB  - A 28-year-old male patient with occipito-atlanto-axial instability underwent a 
      cervical fusion with posterior technique. Post-operatively, the endotracheal tube 
      (ETT) was removed, and the patient was transferred to the intensive care unit. 
      After transfer, an upper airway obstruction developed and reintubations with a 
      laryngoscope were attempted but failed. We inserted a #4 proseal laryngeal mask 
      airway (LMA) and passed a 5.0 mm ETT through the LMA with the aid of a fiberoptic 
      bronchoscope. We passed a tube exchanger through the 5.0 mm ETT and exchanged it 
      with a 7.5 mm ETT. This method may be a useful alternative for difficult tracheal 
      intubations.
