VI  - 2014
DP  - 2014 Apr 4
TI  - Lung adenocarcinoma masquerading as refractory Klebsiella pneumoniae.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2013-202993 [doi]
LID - bcr2013202993
AB  - We report the case of a middle-aged man where a diagnosis of Klebsiella 
      pneumoniae obscured the underlying malignancy. The patient was hospitalised for 
      management of a presumed refractory community-acquired pneumonia with 
      radiological features of right lower lobe consolidation. Bronchoscopy did not 
      identify an endobronchial lesion and washings grew K pneumoniae. CT-guided 
      fine-needle aspirate samples did not detect any malignancy. However, despite 
      appropriate antibiotic treatment there was no improvement in the patient's 
      clinical condition. Consequently, a CT-guided lung core biopsy was performed to 
      obtain more tissue for histopathology, which was diagnostic of primary lung 
      adenocarcinoma. This case highlights the need to continue to investigate a 
      patient who is not progressing as clinically appropriate to their original 
      diagnosis.
