TI  - Metastatic hepatic clear cell carcinoma presenting as lump in the hilum of the 
      lung: a case report and review of the literature.
PG  - E232-5
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.11.31 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of a 52-year-old Chinese woman with a history of primary hepatic 
      cell carcinoma who presented with chest pain, cough, expectoration and bloody 
      phlegm. Chest computer tomography (CT) revealed a 6.2 cm × 6.8 cm shallow 
      lobulated irregular shaped mass in the hilum of the right lung. Bronchoscopy and 
      CT guided lung biopsy was performed. Histopathological and immunohistochemical 
      examinations of biopsies revealed the diagnosis of lung metastatic hepatic clear 
      cell carcinoma. This case is thought to be extremely rare.
