TI  - Pneumomediastinum and (bilateral) pneumothorax after high energy trauma: 
      Indications for emergency bronchoscopy.
PG  - 9-11
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2014.06.003 [doi]
AB  - High energy trauma may cause injury to tracheobronchial structures. This is 
      sometimes difficult to diagnose immediately. Pneumomediastinum and (bilateral) 
      pneumothorax seen on a CT-scan of the thorax may suggest possible damage to 
      central airways. Emergency bronchoscopy should be performed to detect and locate 
      a possible tracheobronchial injury.
