TI  - Training: simulating pediatric airway.
PG  - 993-1003
LID - S0031-3955(13)00061-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.pcl.2013.04.002 [doi]
AB  - Training in the management of pediatric airway cases has been limited by the 
      number of cases and by the involved risks to the child. Simulation is an 
      alternative and accessible means to practice that complex psychomotor task in a 
      safe and reproducible environment. A high-fidelity baby mannequin provides an 
      acceptable airway anatomic resemblance combined with measurable respiratory and 
      cardiovascular parameters, allowing practice to be interactive and challenging. 
      The availability of simulation laboratories within hospitals and the development 
      of pathology-inspired accessories for the mannequins will determine the rate of 
      adherence of ENT departments to this evolving field of simulation-based 
      education.
