TI  - Intrathoracic dislocation of the inferior pole of the scapula following 
      thoracotomy.
PG  - 450-2
AB  - Intrathoracic dislocation of the scapula is extremely rare. We present the case 
      of a 64 year old man who underwent a lung transplant for emphysema via a standard 
      posterior thoracotomy approach. Four weeks later, following a bronchoscopy, he 
      experienced severe pain and restriction of movement in his shoulder. CT scans 
      revealed intrathoracic dislocation of the inferior angle of the scapula. Two 
      manipulations under anaesthesia were unsuccessful and formal exploration required 
      with closure of the intercostal defect. We describe our surgical technique.
