TI  - Minimally invasive in vivo human lung tissue bioimpedance measurements during the 
      bronchoscopy procedure.
PG  - 130-3
LID - 10.1109/EMBC.2012.6345888 [doi]
AB  - Respiratory diseases, which include diseases of the lung, pleura, bronchial tree, 
      trachea, upper respiratory tract and of the respiratory muscles and nerves, are a 
      common and important cause of illness and death among the population. 
      Experimental evidences have shown that tissue lesions have different electrical 
      properties compared with normal tissue. Therefore, lung tissues lesions may be 
      differentiated from lung normal tissue by comparing the tissue passive electrical 
      properties. The manuscript reports a feasibility study for minimally invasive in 
      vivo human lung tissue tetrapolar bioimpedance measurements using a catheter 
      during the bronchoscopy procedure based on multisine Electrical Impedance 
      Spectroscopy (EIS) at 10 kHz - 1 MHz.
