TI  - Extracorporeal membrane oxygenation used in a massive lung bleeding following 
      pulmonary endarterectomy.
PG  - 299-302
AB  - The authors present a case of massive lung bleeding following pulmonary 
      endarterectomy (PEA) that was treated with peripheral veno-venous extracorporeal 
      membrane oxygenation (VV ECMO). The patient repeatedly underwent bronchoscopy for 
      airway blood clot obstruction and finally was successfully weaned off the 
      support. The authors discuss the indications for ECMO in treatment of the most 
      serious complications following PEA, and emphasize the importance of 
      echocardiographic evaluation of the right ventricular function in relation to the 
      indicated type of extracorporeal support. Anticoagulation strategy for patients 
      shortly after the major surgery connected to ECMO is also discussed.
