TI  - Anesthetic challenges in managing a case of type III laryngo-tracheo-esophageal 
      cleft.
PG  - 514-6
LID - 10.4103/0970-9185.101945 [doi]
AB  - Laryngo-tracheo-esophageal cleft (LTEC) is a rare congenital anomaly 
      characterized by failure of fusion of the cricoid cartilage posteriorly and 
      incomplete development of the tracheo-esophageal septum. Securing the airway 
      during anesthesia in patients with LTEC, especially in the severe forms is a 
      challenge. We describe the anesthetic management and the airway challenges in a 
      neonate with type III LTEC who underwent bronchoscopy and repair of LTEC.
