TI  - Proptosis during flexible bronchoscopy.
PG  - 249-50
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e31825ceac6 [doi]
AB  - Bronchoscopy has been described as a safe procedure with a low rate of 
      complications. We present a case of a 48-year-old woman who underwent flexible 
      bronchoscopy for chronic cough. Immediately after the procedure, she developed 
      proptosis of the left eye that required urgent attention. It resolved with 
      medical treatment alone and the patient was discharged without any long-term 
      complications.
