TI  - Alternatives to resectional surgery for infectious disease of the lung: from 
      embolization to thoracoplasty.
PG  - 413-29
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2012.05.001 [doi]
AB  - Surgical treatment of lung diseases is based on removal of the affected lung 
      tissue, achieved by atypical or anatomic lung resection. Infectious lung diseases 
      are generally treated by medical therapy, including medications, chest 
      physiotherapy, bronchoscopic toilet, and respiratory rehabilitation. Surgical 
      management of infectious disease of the lung is integrated in the multispecialty 
      care. This article focuses exclusively on nonresectional surgery and other 
      alternatives to lung resection and addresses bacterial infection and fungal 
      disease of the lung.
