TI  - Mediastinal goiter diagnosed by functional imaging.
LID - 10.3402/ljm.v7i0.15693 [doi]
AB  - A 63-year-old asymptomatic woman with cured Hodgkin diseases presented for 
      restaging. The chest computed tomography showed a mass at the right side of the 
      upper mediastinum. The benignity and the origin of the tissue were unknown. 
      First, we performed a bronchoscopy-guided biopsy but without success. In the next 
      step, we initiated radionuclide imaging with technetium-99m pertechnetate 
      (Tc-99m) and radioiodine (I-123). Low uptake of Tc-99m and intense accumulation 
      of I-123 after 2 and 24 h to the mediastinal mass suggested that the mass was a 
      mediastinal goiter. Based on iodine uptake and the fact that our patient had no 
      symptoms of tracheal compression, we decide to go for a radioiodine therapy.
