TI  - Endoscopic cryosurgical resection of pulmonary hamartoma with flexible 
      bronchoscopy.
PG  - 307-10
LID - 10.5090/kjtcs.2011.44.4.307 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary hamartoma is one of the most common benign lung tumors. Well-known 
      conventional methods of treatment for lung hamartomas include VATS enucleation or 
      wedge resection, bronchoplasty, and others. Here we present a case of 
      endobronchial hamartoma that was successfully treated with cryosurgery by 
      flexible bronchoscopy.
