TI  - A case of adult T cell leukemia/lymphoma presenting as severe tracheal stenosis.
PG  - 2637-41
AB  - A 57-year-old woman was referred to our hospital for further examination of a 
      tracheal stenosis shown on computed tomography findings. Bronchoscopy revealed 
      multiple protruding tumors in the lumen of the trachea. Cytological findings of 
      the cell block material from pleural effusion indicated that the T-cell lymphoma 
      was composed of pleomorphic lymphoid cells. Serum human T-cell leukemia virus 
      type 1 antibody was positive and supported the clinical diagnosis of ATLL. 
      Systemic chemotherapy induced the remarkable improvement of the lesions, the 
      infiltrative lung shadow and the soft tissue neoplasm. We report a rare case of 
      adult T cell leukemia/lymphoma (ATLL) with endobronchial involvement.
