TI  - Unexpected difficulty in ventilating the lungs after tracheal intubation -A case 
      report-.
PG  - 437-9
LID - 10.4097/kjae.2011.60.6.437 [doi]
AB  - We experienced difficulty in ventilating the lungs of a patient after tracheal 
      intubation. After intubation, an insufficient amount of tidal volume (V(T)) was 
      delivered to the patient and the fiberoptic bronchoscopic examination identified 
      partial abutment of the endotracheal tube (ETT) orifice against the tracheal 
      wall. After various attempts to correctly place the ETT, a double-lumen 
      endotracheal tube was placed to achieve a sufficient V(T). It is important to 
      notice that even an appropriately placed ETT may get obstructed due to the left 
      sided bevel at its tip.
