TI  - An endobronchial chondromatous hamartoma.
PG  - 292-4
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e318222a6ab [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial chondromatous hamartoma is a very rare benign lung tumor. We report 
      a 68-year-old male patient who presented with a 2-year history of worsening 
      shortness of breath and wheeze, misdiagnosed as having asthma. Computed 
      tomographic scan showed a lesion in the right lower lobe bronchus, and 
      bronchoscopy confirmed the presence of an endobronchial tumor, which was 
      completely excised. Microscopic examination of the tumor showed features of an 
      endobronchial chondromatous hamartoma. The patient made an excellent recovery.
