TI  - [Haemoptysis revealing tracheobronchial amyloidosis].
PG  - 109-12
LID - 10.1016/j.pneumo.2010.02.003 [doi]
AB  - The authors report the case of a 68-year-old man complaining of haemoptysis and 
      breathlessness. Bronchoscopy revealed a budding formation in tracheal 
      bifurcation. Multiple biopsies were performed and concluded as to AL type 
      amyloidosis. Tracheobronchial amyloidosis is an uncommon localised form of 
      amyloidosis that can simulate lung cancer.
