TI  - Chlorine-induced extensive tracheobronchial necrosis concomitantly 
      benzene-induced pancytopenia presented with severe pneumonia.
PG  - 439-43
AB  - We report a case of 25-year-old woman with severe tracheobronchial necrosis 
      caused by chlorine released from a mixture household cleaning agents. She 
      subsequently exposed benzene while she was fixing the seats with benzene 
      containing gum. The case was found interesting with its history, delayed 
      diagnosis, bronchoscopic features, and fatal outcome. We presented its 
      bronchoscopic and pathological images which has not been shown in the literature 
      up to date.
