TI  - Bronchoscopic electrocautery therapy of a solitary endobronchial extramedullary 
      plasmacytoma.
PG  - 435-8
AB  - Extramedullary plasmacytomas are rare tumors. In majority of cases tumors arise 
      in the head and neck region and endobronchial localization is extremely rare. The 
      treatment is usually resection alone or combination of surgery with radiotherapy. 
      Herein we present a case of solitary endobronchial plasmacytoma which was 
      resected with bronchoscopic electrocautery, because of extremely rare occurrence 
      of solitary endobronchial plasmacytoma and also the successful outcome of 
      bronchoscopic electrocautery therapy.
