TI  - Endobronchial mucosal blanching due to a post-lung transplantation pulmonary 
      artery stenosis.
PG  - e27-8
LID - 10.1016/j.ejcts.2010.10.021 [doi]
AB  - A 45-year-old woman underwent a bronchoscopy shortly after lung transplantation. 
      The airway mucosal appearance significantly differed between both lungs, with a 
      pale aspect of the left bronchial tree. Computed tomography (CT) and perfusion 
      scan confirmed a left pulmonary artery stenosis, improving with conservative 
      treatment.
