TI  - Video RIFL: a rigid flexible laryngoscope to facilitate airway management.
PG  - 642-7
LID - 10.1016/j.jclinane.2009.10.019 [doi]
AB  - The video RIFL (rigid flexible laryngoscope) is an airway management adjunct 
      designed to facilitate endotracheal intubation. It is a novel stylet-based 
      laryngoscope that incorporates a complementary metal oxide sensor distal chip 
      imaging system and real-time articulation tip. The device combines features 
      desired in fiberoptic bronchoscopy as well as in video laryngoscopy. Four cases 
      involving its use in difficult airway management are presented.
