TI  - [Chronic cough as the presenting feature of temporal arteritis].
PG  - e76-8
LID - 10.1016/j.revmed.2010.06.009 [doi]
AB  - We report a 70-year-old woman who presented with a chronic cough of 3-month 
      duration, secondarily associated with fever and weight loss. She had no other 
      symptoms. Physical examination was unremarkable and laboratory tests showed an 
      increase level of acute phase reactants. Thoracic, abdominal and sinus computed 
      tomographic scan was normal and bronchoscopy showed a non specific mucosa 
      inflammation. Despite the absence of characteristic manifestations of temporal 
      arteritis, a temporal artery biopsy was performed and disclosed evidence of 
      typical temporal arteritis.
