PG  - 60-3
AB  - The authors describe a successful case of esophageal fistula being cured in a 
      patient with complicated tuberculosis of intrathoracic lymph nodes. They show it 
      possible to medically cure the fistula via temporary esophageal stenting, which 
      in combination with therapeutic bronchoscopies enables prompt fistula healing, 
      without resorting to surgical treatment.
