TI  - Primary bronchial granular cell tumor in an adult male.
PG  - 193-6
LID - 10.5090/kjtcs.2014.47.2.193 [doi]
AB  - We report a rare case of granular cell tumor arising in the left lower lobe (LLL) 
      bronchus with secondary obstructive change in a 60-year-old male. The patient was 
      found to have a nodule in the LLL on a computed tomography scan, three months 
      prior to his presentation to the Asan Medical Center. Bronchoscopic biopsies 
      revealed a granular cell tumor. After undergoing LLL lobectomy with 
      bronchoplasty, the patient has not experienced any tumor recurrence.
