TI  - Two tracheal BALT lymphoma patients successfully treated with chemotherapy 
      including rituximab.
PG  - 144-6
LID - S2212-5345(13)00112-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.resinv.2013.07.006 [doi]
AB  - Bronchus-associated lymphoid tissue (BALT) lymphoma of the trachea, an important 
      differential diagnosis for tracheal tumors, is a rare disease with characteristic 
      bronchoscopic findings. In this study, we reviewed 2 cases of patients who were 
      symptomatic at the time of diagnosis, with tumors in the trachea and left main 
      bronchus, putting them at high risk for asphyxia. Chemotherapies including 
      rituximab were administered, and complete remission was confirmed in both cases. 
      Because tracheal tumors often have a pernicious course, it might be beneficial to 
      initiate a chemotherapeutic treatment regimen instead of adopting the 
      "wait-and-see" approach in patients with symptomatic tracheal BALT lymphoma.
