TI  - Fracture and aspiration of a tracheostomy tube.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2013-203232 [doi]
LID - bcr2013203232
AB  - A 70-year-old woman presented with a fracture and aspiration of her polyvinyl 
      chloride tracheostomy tube. Her chest X-ray showed that a foreign body was lodged 
      in the right main bronchus. She was otherwise asymptomatic. The foreign body was 
      removed under general anaesthesia using a flexible bronchoscope. The patient 
      developed pneumonia after the procedure and was admitted to the intensive care 
      unit. She was discharged home 5 days after the event with no permanent 
      complications.
