TI  - Tracheal diverticulum: a rare cause of hoarseness of the voice.
PG  - e29-31
LID - S0003-4975(13)02156-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2013.09.069 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal diverticulum is a rare benign disease also known as paratracheal air 
      cyst. Mostly these are asymptomatic and are discovered incidentally on radiologic 
      examination of the chest. Common symptoms are cough, recurrent respiratory tract 
      infections, and sometimes dysphagia. Herein we report a rare case of hoarseness 
      of voice caused by tracheal diverticulum. Computed tomography scan of neck 
      revealed a large tracheal diverticulum, probably compressing the recurrent 
      laryngeal nerve as bronchoscopy showed impaired right vocal cord movement. Two 
      weeks after diverticulectomy, the patient's voice returned to normal.
