TI  - Severe propofol-associated dystonia in a dog.
PG  - 471-4
AB  - A 2-year-old castrated dog was presented for chronic coughing that was evaluated 
      with bronchoscopy following intravenous boluses of propofol. During recovery the 
      dog developed severe rigidity of muscles of the neck and thoracic limbs, which 
      was unresponsive to treatment but subsided over 25 minutes. A presumptive 
      diagnosis of propofol-associated dystonia was made. The clinical characteristics 
      and theorized pathophysiology of propofol-associated dystonia are discussed.
