TI  - Bronchoscopy as a rescue therapy in patients with status asthmaticus: Two case 
      reports and review of literature.
PG  - 327-30
LID - 10.4103/1658-354X.115323 [doi]
AB  - Management of status asthmaticus requires more than guidelines-guided therapy. 
      Occasionally, uncommon therapeutic interventions and procedures may provide 
      significant benefits. The role of bronchoscopy in fatal asthma is still not 
      clearly defined. We illustrate two cases of severe status asthmaticus on 
      mechanical ventilation who showed remarkable improvement after therapeutic 
      bronchoscopy.
