TI  - Adult Henoch-Schönlein purpura associated with small cell lung cancer: A case 
      report and review of the literature.
PG  - 1927-1930
AB  - The present study reports the case of a 53-year-old male who had been suffering 
      from coughing and the presence of a blood-streaked sputum for >1 month. Chest 
      computed tomography (CT) and a bronchoscopic brush smear were performed. The 
      patient was subsequently diagnosed with small cell lung cancer (limited stage). 
      The patient developed polyarthritis, abdominal pain, diarrhea and a purpuric rash 
      at 14 days post thoracotomy surgery for lung cancer. Henoch-Schönlein purpura 
      (HSP) was diagnosed based on the clinical symptoms. The patient received 
      chemotherapy with steroid therapy, which resulted in complete remission of the 
      HSP.
