TI  - Intratracheal inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour mimicking severe acute asthma.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2013-010232 [doi]
LID - bcr2013010232
AB  - A 3-year-old boy presented with severe airway obstruction which was diagnosed as 
      asthma. He improved but had repeated episodes of severe airway obstruction. On 
      clinical examination, he had a tracheal cough and monophonic wheezing. Imaging 
      revealed a large lesion in the distal part of the trachea which was confirmed by 
      bronchoscopy. The lesion was surgically removed. Histology revealed features 
      characteristic of an inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour. Following the resection 
      there is no recurrence of the lesion.
