TI  - Use of nasopharyngeal aspirate for diagnosis of pneumocystis pneumonia.
PG  - 1570-4
LID - 10.1128/JCM.03264-12 [doi]
AB  - Quantitative PCR on nasopharyngeal aspirate (NPA) can achieve high sensitivity 
      and specificity in diagnosing Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) compared to 
      microscopic examination of bronchoscopic specimens in a population with low HIV 
      prevalence. Since NPA is a minimally invasive procedure, it is ideal as a 
      screening test for PCP.
