TI  - Tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica in a 5 year-old girl.
PG  - 985-6
AB  - Tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica (TO) is considered an orphan disease 
      with exceptional occurrence in children. We report a 5 year old female child who 
      was referred to us with chronic cough and recurrent pneumonia. After several 
      investigations, bronchoscopy showed multiple nodules in the tracheobronchial 
      lumen, whose distribution was consistent with TO. The patient was followed for 
      four years, with no change in the pattern of the disease.
