TI  - Sudden atelectasis and respiratory failure in a neutropenic patient: atypical 
      presentation of pseudomembranous necrotizing bronchial aspergillosis.
PG  - 463-6
LID - 10.3904/kjim.2012.27.4.463 [doi]
AB  - Pseudomembranous necrotizing bronchial aspergillosis (PNBA) is a rare form of 
      invasive aspergillosis with a very poor prognosis. The symptoms are non-specific, 
      and the necrotizing plugs cause airway obstruction. Atelectasis and respiratory 
      failure can be the initial manifestations. Recently, we treated an 
      immunocompromised patient with PNBA, who presented with a sudden onset of 
      atelectasis and acute respiratory failure. There were no preceding signs except 
      for a mild cough and one febrile episode. Bronchoscopy revealed PNBA, and 
      Aspergillus nidulans was cultured from the bronchial wash.
