TI  - Placement of a double-lumen tube using LMA C Trach and an exchanger catheter in 
      difficult airway intubation -A case report-.
PG  - 565-7
LID - 10.4097/kjae.2012.62.6.565 [doi]
AB  - During insertion of the double lumen tube in patients with cervical vertebral 
      fixation, the cervical neutral position should be maintained. Although flexible 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopic intubation is the gold standard, novel techniques are 
      needed to facilitate intubation of patients with cervical vertebral fixation in 
      neutral position according to institutional capabilities. In this case report, 
      insertion of the double lumen tube in the neutral position using LMA CTrach and 
      an airway exchanger catheter in a thoracotomy patient with extremely limited head 
      and neck motion due to fixation of the cervical vertebrae is presented.
