TI  - [Schwannoma occurred in the right upper bronchial inlet; report of a case].
PG  - 594-7
AB  - A 47-year-old woman was treated at a local hospital for obstructive pneumonia in 
      February 2011. A computed tomography(CT)scan revealed a nodule obstructing the 
      right upper bronchus. Histological diagnosis could not be established by biopsy 
      under the bronchoscopic examination. She was referred to our hospital for further 
      treatment. Since accumulation of fluoro-2-deoxy-D-glucose(FDG)was noted by 
      positron emission tomography(PET)[standardized uptake value(SUV)max 5.67/7.52], 
      primary lung cancer was suspected and right upper sleeve lobectomy was performed. 
      Pathology during surgery suggested the tumor to be schwannoma. Postoperative 
      course was uneventful.
