DP  - 2013 Mar
TI  - Delayed pneumothorax after bronchoscopy in a lung transplant patient.
PG  - e18-9
LID - 10.4187/respcare.01842 [doi]
AB  - Lung transplant patients commonly undergo transbronchial biopsy to evaluate for 
      rejection. Post-biopsy radiographs are used to exclude pneumothorax, one of the 
      most common major complications. We report a lung transplant patient who 
      developed a pneumothorax 5 months after transbronchial biopsy, with multiple 
      intervening chest computed tomograms documenting that the pneumothorax developed 
      from the biopsy site. This case illustrates that in transplant patients 
      transbronchial biopsy can evolve to pneumothorax several months later, despite 
      normal post-biopsy radiographs.
