TI  - Percutaneous retrieval of coiled double-J stent from renal pelvis after 
      Anderson-Hynes pyeloplasty: report of two cases.
PG  - e19-22
LID - 10.1016/j.jpurol.2012.01.008 [doi]
AB  - Double-J (DJ) ureteral stents are routinely placed for internal urinary diversion 
      post renal pyeloplasty. Malfunction of the stent may occur due to migration, 
      necessitating removal. Upward migration of a DJ stent is rarely encountered in 
      urologic practice when a ureteroscope is used to retrieve the stent. However, 
      retrieval of upwardly migrated stents through ureteroscopy may be challenging in 
      the pediatric population, especially in postoperative cases. We report two 
      pediatric cases of post Anderson-Hynes pyeloplasty in whom the DJ stents were 
      found coiled up in the renal pelvis and were retrieved successfully through 
      percutaneous nephrostomy using semirigid bronchoscopic forceps.
