TI  - Kaposi sarcoma with laryngeal, tracheal, and parenchymal involvement.
PG  - 259-60
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e318222a1b8 [doi]
AB  - The exclusive respiratory involvement by Kaposi sarcoma is rare, especially in 
      the upper airway. When present, it could lead to severe airway compromise. We 
      present the case of a human immunodeficiency virus infection-positive male 
      patient who presents with dyspnea and stridor, and was found to have bilateral 
      vocal cord paralysis and stenosis of the upper airway due to laryngeal and 
      tracheal involvement by Kaposi sarcoma. The patient underwent bronchoscopy for 
      both diagnostic and therapeutic intentions.
