AB  - A 48-year-old man presented with recurrent bronchopulmonary infections of many 
      years' standing. The diagnosis of tracheobronchomegaly (Mounier-Kuhn syndrome) 
      was based on CT examination and subsequent bronchoscopy. Since lung 
      transplantation was not considered advisable, a biluminal stent was inserted to 
      prevent bronchial collapse.
