IS  - 1022-386X (Linking)
VI  - 20
IP  - 6
DP  - 2010 Jun
TI  - Tracheal schwannoma: a rare tracheal tumour.
PG  - 410-1
AB  - Primary tracheal tumours are histologically similar but 100 times less common 
      than main stem tumours. We report a case of primary tracheal schwannoma in a 
      middle aged man. He had chronic cough for 2 years, and developed hemoptysis and 
      stridor in the days preceding to presentation. He was treated by resection of the 
      tumour and primary anatomosis of the trachea. The patient recovered well after 
      surgery and had a near normal PEFR after one and a half year of follow-up and 
      bronchoscopic examination excluded any recurrence.
